Emerging Market Opportunities
Solid-State Battery Development
The development of solid-state batteries is creating demand for adhesives compatible with new cell architectures and electrolyte materials. Manufacturers are investigating specialized bonding solutions that can accommodate different thermal, mechanical, and chemical requirements. Suppliers able to develop materials for emerging solid-state battery production may gain opportunities as commercialization advances.

Battery Recycling and Debondable Adhesives
Battery recycling is creating interest in adhesives that can be selectively removed during disassembly. Thermally reversible and solvent-debondable formulations could make it easier to separate battery components and recover valuable materials. These solutions may support circular manufacturing strategies and improve the efficiency of battery recycling operations.

